<body data-time="all">
  <header class="site"><div class="wrap bar"><a class="brand" href="/">Vault <b>Human</b></a><nav class="navlinks"><a href="/#how">How it works</a><a href="/method/">The method</a><a href="/#pricing">Pricing</a><a href="/#russ">About Russ</a><a class="btn btn-acc" href="#" data-open-form>Start free</a></nav></div></header>
  <main>
    <section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="timeword"><span class="tw past">Past</span><span class="tw present">Present</span><span class="tw future">Future</span></div>
      <p class="eyebrow">How we coach</p>
      <h1>One method. <em>Your whole life.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Most coaching picks one thing: your habits, your mindset, your body, your money. We don't think a life comes in pieces. So we built a method that doesn't either.</p>
      <div class="ctarow"><a class="btn btn-acc" href="#" data-open-form>Start free — 7 days of lessons</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="#lists">See what it's built from</a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">What makes it different</p><h2>Integrative. Holistic. Human.</h2><p class="lede">Three words that get used loosely. Here is exactly what we mean by them.</p></div>
      <div class="pains">
        <div class="pain"><h3>Integrative</h3><p>We did not invent a philosophy. We read the whole field, 360 ways people have tried to become whole, from ancient scripture to modern psychology, and put the best of each in order. Nothing is ours. The order is.</p></div>
        <div class="pain"><h3>Holistic</h3><p>Mind and body are one year, not two programs. 360 lessons for the mind. 180 for the body: fuel, fitness, sleep, breath, rest. The same morning, the same coach, the same notebook.</p></div>
        <div class="pain"><h3>Human</h3><p>Vault is the action. Human is the person. A real person reads what you write every night. The method only works because someone is listening.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec dark" id="why"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Why 360 and 180</p><h2>Everything that has ever helped a person, in one year.</h2></div>
      <div class="two" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px">
        <div class="row" style="background:var(--dark2);border-radius:10px;padding:26px"><h3 style="color:#fff">The 360 · the mind, the heart, the spirit</h3><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.75);margin-top:10px">Three hundred and sixty teachings, each sourced to a named teacher, text or tradition. Psychology and recovery. Mystics, poets and sages. Scripture from the Abrahamic, Indian, East Asian, Indigenous and ancient worlds. Leadership and work. The body, the breath, the nervous system. Habits and performance. Each one has a date, an author, and a reason it made the list. We did not leave the spiritual out to be safe. It is the largest part.</p></div>
        <div class="row" style="background:var(--dark2);border-radius:10px;padding:26px"><h3 style="color:#fff">The 180 · fuel and fitness</h3><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.75);margin-top:10px">One hundred and eighty ways people have fed, trained, rested and healed a body. Modern protocols with trial evidence. Ancient and traditional medicine. The foodways and fasts of living religions. Strength, endurance, mobility, sleep, heat and cold, sobriety. Every other day, one of them, with the walk and the table as the two that never change.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="constant" style="margin-top:34px">Four verbs hold all 540: <span style="color:var(--acc)">Learn</span> · <span style="color:var(--acc)">Love</span> · <span style="color:var(--acc)">Live</span> · <span style="color:var(--acc)">Listen</span></p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">How the year moves</p><h2>Eleven rooms. Nine doors. One key a day.</h2><p class="lede">Think of the year as a house. You walk through it one room at a time, and each door opens when the habit holds, not when the calendar says so.</p></div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><div class="n">1–5</div><h3>Our order</h3><p>Months one to five. Fire, Breath, Silence, Order, Stewardship: the rooms that settle a person as a self. Everyone walks these first.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="n">6</div><h3>The rest</h3><p>Month six. No new lessons. You keep the walk and the table, and you write. This is where most programs fail; it is where ours turns.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="n">7–12</div><h3>Your order</h3><p>Months seven to twelve. The Face, the Name, the Table, the Watch, the Tomorrow: the rooms that turn a person toward others. You choose the sequence. Your own tradition is welcome back here.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec" id="human"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">The human part</p><h2>Vault is the action.<br>Human is the person.</h2><p class="lede">Every lesson ends with one small thing to do, and every night ends with three lines in your own hand. Those lines are read by a person, not a model. That is the whole difference between information and coaching, and it is the part we will not automate.</p></div>
      <div class="pains">
        <div class="pain"><h3>A real reader</h3><p>Your coach reads your notes before your session. Nothing you write disappears into a dashboard.</p></div>
        <div class="pain"><h3>A real circle</h3><p>Six people, once a week, who are walking the same rooms. Listening is the fourth verb for a reason.</p></div>
        <div class="pain"><h3>A real tradition</h3><p>We do not replace your faith or your practice. The second half of the year is built so it can come back in, as your own choice.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec dark" id="lists"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">See the whole thing</p><h2>The lists are public.</h2><p class="lede">We are not hiding the curriculum. Every teaching and every protocol is named, dated and explained. Read them. Argue with them. Then start.</p></div>
      <div class="tl-cards"><a class="tlc green" href="/the-360/"><div class="when">Mind · heart · spirit</div><h3>The 360</h3><p>Every teaching, by category, with its source and the one line that says what it asks of you.</p><span>Read the 360 →</span></a><a class="tlc brown" href="/the-180/"><div class="when">Fuel · fitness · rest</div><h3>The 180</h3><p>Every protocol and tradition, by category, with its source and what it asks of your body.</p><span>Read the 180 →</span></a><a class="tlc navy" href="#" data-open-form><div class="when">Day one</div><h3>Start free</h3><p>Seven days of lessons, one each morning. A real person replies with the first.</p><span>Start free →</span></a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec final"><div class="wrap">
      <h2>One method. Your whole life.</h2><p class="lede">Sign up tonight. Your first lesson is in your inbox at 7 a.m.</p>
      <div class="ctarow"><a class="btn btn-acc" href="#" data-open-form>Start free — 7 days</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="/#pricing">See pricing</a></div>
    </div></section>
  </main>
